1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,513
In this lesson, you'll learn to
work with many contacts at once.

2
00:00:04,513 --> 00:00:09,089
You'll pick out a group with a smart
list or a filter, then tag, message,

3
00:00:09,089 --> 00:00:12,412
enrol and export everyone
in it in just a few clicks.

4
00:00:13,296 --> 00:00:15,104
Bulk actions save you hours.

5
00:00:15,104 --> 00:00:17,623
Instead of opening contacts one by one,

6
00:00:17,623 --> 00:00:20,917
you select a group and act
on all of them together.

7
00:00:20,917 --> 00:00:25,373
Tag a group, message them, add them
to an automation, or export them.

8
00:00:25,373 --> 00:00:28,861
It all starts with getting
the right people on screen.

9
00:00:29,711 --> 00:00:31,699
Smart lists are perfect for this.

10
00:00:31,699 --> 00:00:35,676
Here's our Reactivation list:
patients we haven't seen in a while.

11
00:00:35,676 --> 00:00:39,351
It updates itself whenever
someone gets the reactivation tag.

12
00:00:40,202 --> 00:00:42,430
You can also build a group on the fly.

13
00:00:42,430 --> 00:00:45,712
Let's filter for everyone
interested in teeth whitening,

14
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:48,350
because we're about to
run a whitening offer.

15
00:00:50,032 --> 00:00:55,152
Tick the box in the header to select everyone
in the list, or tick individual rows.

16
00:00:55,152 --> 00:00:59,285
A bulk action bar appears, showing
how many people you've selected.

17
00:01:00,135 --> 00:01:03,889
First, let's tag them, so we
can track who got this offer.

18
00:01:03,889 --> 00:01:06,024
Click Add tag and choose the tag.

19
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:08,937
It's added to every
selected contact at once.

20
00:01:08,937 --> 00:01:13,596
Later, you can filter by this tag to
see exactly who received the offer,

21
00:01:13,596 --> 00:01:14,567
and who booked.

22
00:01:15,418 --> 00:01:17,160
Now let's send them a text.

23
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:20,901
Select them again, click Send
SMS, and write your message.

24
00:01:20,901 --> 00:01:24,385
Placeholders like first name
make every text personal,

25
00:01:24,385 --> 00:01:26,965
even when it goes to hundreds of people.

26
00:01:27,781 --> 00:01:30,477
Choose drip mode to send in small batches,

27
00:01:30,477 --> 00:01:33,687
so replies come in at a
pace your team can handle.

28
00:01:33,687 --> 00:01:39,079
And don't worry about opt-outs: Kyntlo skips
anyone with Do Not Disturb switched on.

29
00:01:39,079 --> 00:01:40,106
Then click Send.

30
00:01:40,956 --> 00:01:44,886
A quick note: text messaging is
included from the Growth plan.

31
00:01:44,886 --> 00:01:48,436
On Starter, you can still
send bulk emails the same way,

32
00:01:48,436 --> 00:01:51,288
using the Send email
button right next to it.

33
00:01:52,138 --> 00:01:57,430
Add to workflow enrols everyone in an
automation, which we'll build in module 9.

34
00:01:57,430 --> 00:02:01,267
And Export downloads the
selected contacts as a .csv file,

35
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:03,384
with the columns you're viewing.

36
00:02:03,384 --> 00:02:07,816
It's handy for backups, or for
sharing a list with your accountant.

37
00:02:08,665 --> 00:02:12,802
Every bulk action is logged under
Bulk Actions, with who started it,

38
00:02:12,802 --> 00:02:15,662
how many contacts it
touched, and its progress.

39
00:02:15,662 --> 00:02:19,677
If something doesn't look right,
this is the first place to check.

40
00:02:19,677 --> 00:02:24,301
Long-running sends, like drip messages,
show their progress here as they go.

41
00:02:25,152 --> 00:02:26,260
Here's a pro tip.

42
00:02:26,260 --> 00:02:29,714
Before you send a bulk
message to hundreds of people,

43
00:02:29,714 --> 00:02:34,602
add yourself as a contact with the same
tag, and send it to just you first.

44
00:02:34,602 --> 00:02:38,056
Check the wording, the links
and the personalisation.

45
00:02:38,056 --> 00:02:39,685
Then send it to everyone.

46
00:02:40,538 --> 00:02:41,269
Great work!

47
00:02:41,269 --> 00:02:46,253
In the last lesson of this module,
we'll keep your database clean: grouping

48
00:02:46,253 --> 00:02:51,635
contacts by company, merging duplicates,
and restoring anyone deleted by mistake.
